{"id":"heart-character-of-the-unrenewed","name":"Heart, Character Of The Unrenewed","aliases":["Heart"],"sources":["torrey","easton"],"topics":["torrey:heart-character-of-the-unrenewed"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Heart","text":"According to the Bible, the heart is the centre not only of spiritual activity, but of all the operations of human life. “Heart” and “soul” are often used interchangeably (Deut. 6:5; 26:16; comp. Matt. 22:37; Mark 12:30, 33), but this is not generally the case. The heart is the “home of the personal life,” and hence a man is designated, according to his heart, wise (1 Kings 3:12, etc.), pure (Ps. 24:4; Matt. 5:8, etc.), upright and righteous (Gen. 20:5, 6; Ps. 11:2; 78:72), pious and good (Luke 8:15), etc. In these and such passages the word “soul” could not be substituted for “heart.” The heart is also the seat of the conscience (Rom. 2:15). It is naturally wicked (Gen. 8:21), and hence it contaminates the whole life and character (Matt. 12:34; 15:18; comp. Eccl. 8:11; Ps. 73:7). Hence the heart must be changed, regenerated (Ezek. 36:26; 11:19; Ps. 51:10-14), before a man can willingly …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"G2588","lemma":"καρδία","xlit":"kardía","gloss":"the heart","kjv":"heart","count":13,"share":0.19},{"strong":"H3824","lemma":"לֵבָב","xlit":"lêbâb","gloss":"the heart","kjv":"bethink themselves, breast, comfortably, courage","count":10,"share":0.14},{"strong":"H6141","lemma":"עִקֵּשׁ","xlit":"ʻiqqêsh","gloss":"distorted","kjv":"crooked, froward, perverse","count":3,"share":0.04},{"strong":"H5493","lemma":"סוּר","xlit":"çûwr","gloss":"to turn off","kjv":"be, bring, call back, decline","count":5,"share":0.07},{"strong":"H136","lemma":"אֲדֹנָי","xlit":"ʼĂdônây","gloss":"the Lord","kjv":"Lord","count":5,"share":0.07},{"strong":"H200","lemma":"אִוֶּלֶת","xlit":"ʼivveleth","gloss":"silliness","kjv":"folly, foolishly","count":3,"share":0.04}],"verses":["Matt.12.35","Matt.15.8","Mark.7.21","John.13.2","Acts.7.51","Act